Subject: [PATCH] Droidloom: room for the spares of two full-screen windows

A task showing one activity over another on a 1216x2688 panel rotates
ten 13 MB buffers. The 96 MiB spare budget evicted one per frame, the
next use imported it again, and that frame was composed instead of
placed, so direct and composed presentation alternated (black or stale
frames in Spotify's player). Imports reference producer buffers and
allocate nothing, so the budget rises to 256 MiB.
---
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/DroidloomImportRetention.h	2026-11-17 13:33:51.407859095 +0100
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/DroidloomImportRetention.h	2026-11-17 13:33:51.430784020 +0100
@@ -37,7 +37,14 @@
     // A layer that switches between opaque and blended keeps both views of
     // its buffers: three buffers, six views.
     constexpr std::size_t kSpareCount = 12, kSparesPerLayer = 6;
-    constexpr uint64_t kSpareBytes = 96ull * 1024 * 1024;
+    // Two full-screen windows of a task (an activity over another) on a
+    // 1216x2688 panel each rotate five 13 MB buffers: eight spares, 105 MB.
+    // A smaller budget evicted one spare per frame, its next use imported it
+    // again, and every such frame was composed instead of placed: direct and
+    // composed presentation alternated, which shows as black or stale
+    // frames. An import references the producer's buffer; it allocates
+    // nothing, so the budget bounds only host bookkeeping.
+    constexpr uint64_t kSpareBytes = 256ull * 1024 * 1024;
     // Video spares are the decoder's own pool, alive while it plays anyway.
     constexpr std::size_t kVideoSpares = 31;
     constexpr uint64_t kVideoSpareBytes = 256ull * 1024 * 1024;
